  <p class="note">
    The final row validates physical scale. A hand measurement confirmed that the print chain
    preserves dimensions from the generated image to the sheet.
  </p>

  <h2>The stack</h2>

  <h3>In the house</h3>
  <p>
    Raspberry Pi Compute Module 5 on a PoE base board, Raspberry Pi OS. Two 7.5" e-paper displays on
    XIAO ESP32-S3, running a patched TRMNL firmware against our own BYOS server. Epson ET-2870 over
    IPP and eSCL, driverless. Frames 3D printed, units assembled by hand.
  </p>

  <h3>In the cloud</h3>
  <p>
    Microsoft Foundry in the EU for every language, vision and image call, behind a single router
    module that is the only place allowed to import a model SDK. Azure AI Content Safety on
    everything generated and on every inbound image. Container Apps for the API, Cosmos DB, Blob
    Storage, Static Web Apps. Infrastructure as Bicep.
  </p>

  <h3>How it ships</h3>
  <p>
    A push to <code>main</code> publishes the API through GitHub OIDC, a federated credential and a
    user-assigned managed identity. The measured end-to-end time is 1 m 35 s. The runner builds the
    image locally, which lets its resource-scoped roles push to the registry and update the
    container app without permission to reconfigure the registry.
  </p>

  <figure class="narrow">
    <img
      src="/images/kit.jpg"
      width="825"
      height="1100"
      loading="lazy"
      alt="An e-paper panel, an ESP32 board and a battery, before assembly."
    />
    <figcaption>
      What goes into a frame: panel, XIAO ESP32-S3, a 2000 mAh cell, and the ribbon between them.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Boundaries enforced in code</h2>

  <p>
    <code>tests/test_boundaries.py</code> checks the stored schema, panel, browser and prompts for the
    vocabulary of engagement optimisation. Each check was mutation-tested by inserting a violation
    and observing the failure.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>The activity itself provides the reason to continue; the system does not add streaks, daily targets or withheld rewards.</li>
    <li>The scheduler responds to approved activities and their deadlines, rather than absence or time-spent metrics.</li>
    <li>
      The review gate makes the profile available only to the models that write and run an activity.
      User-facing displays, printed sheets and panel pages receive reviewed activity content.
    </li>
    <li>The vision path processes returned sheets. Its schema carries marks or blank, rather than faces, identity, emotion, attention or biometric data.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Parent decisions live in the approval ledger, separate from the generated <code>Proposal</code>.
    The safety gate alone mints the payload type required by user-facing content. These boundaries
    are represented by types and seals, so code that bypasses them fails before it can run.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`}>Why each boundary exists, and what it costs</a
    > · <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/docs/prompts`}>every prompt, whole, as the model receives it</a>
  </p>
</Base>
